-- title:
--   Rational functions of X_H(M) as fractions in a crossing stalk
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \neq 0$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ containing every unit that reduces to $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$, with $M/p \neq 0$, and assume $\mathrm{jqModC}\,\mathbb{Q}$ lies in the $q$-expansion function field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model datum `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and $\rho : R_p \to A$ a lift of the structure map $R_p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with $\rho_O : R_p \to O$, maximal ideal generated by $p$, equipped with $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa(A)$, $j_O : O \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $\iota_A : O \to A$ compatible with $\rho$, $\rho_O$, the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and the residue map; let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two morphisms `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` and `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 1` attached to $\mathfrak{X}$. Let further $O'$ be a discrete valuation domain with $\sigma : O \to O'$ and an injective local homomorphism $\iota_{A'} : O' \to A$ with $\iota_{A'} \circ \sigma = \iota_A$, together with $j_{O'} : O' \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ compatible with $\sigma \circ \rho_O$, with $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ via $\iota_{A'}$, and with the residue map over $\rho$. Write $X_{\mathbb{Q}}$ for the base change of `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $R_p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and $\mathrm{pr}_J$, $\mathrm{pr}_{J'}$, $\mathrm{pr}_{\sigma}$ for the comparison morphisms to `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO`, to `XO (ΓM M H) hj (σ.comp ρO)` and between the latter two, induced by $j_O$, $j_{O'}$ and $\sigma$; let $\mathrm{bc}'$ be the morphism `bcMap` from the fibre over $\kappa(A)$ into `XO (ΓM M H) hj (σ.comp ρO)`, let $x_n'$ be the image of $n$ under the first projection followed by `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` and $\mathrm{bc}'$, let $B$ be the stalk of `XO (ΓM M H) hj (σ.comp ρO)` at $x_n'$, and let $\sigma_B : O' \to B$ be the germ at $x_n'$ of the structure map. Then for every specialisation $\mathrm{hsp}$ of the image in `XO (ΓM M H) hj (σ.comp ρO)`, under `𝔛.eeta` followed by $\mathrm{pr}_{J'}$, of the generic point of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ to $x_n'$, the induced ring homomorphism $\mathrm{emb} : B \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \cdot F(X_H(M))$ — the stalk specialisation map, followed by the stalk maps of $\mathrm{pr}_{J'}$ and of `𝔛.eeta`, followed by the inverse of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{ffEquiv}$ — is injective, satisfies $\mathrm{emb} \circ \sigma_B = \iota \circ j_{O'}$ where $\iota : \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \cdot F(X_H(M))$ is the structure map, and has the property that for every $a$ in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓM M H)` there are $r, s \in B$ with $s \neq 0$ and $\mathrm{coeffEmb}_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}(a) \cdot \mathrm{emb}(s) = \mathrm{emb}(r)$ inside `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`.
--
--   This is the stalk-reading statement at a crossing point of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ over a second coefficient ring: the local ring at the crossing embeds into the geometric function field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \cdot F(X_H(M))$, compatibly with constants, and every rational function of $X_H(M)$ defined over $\mathbb{Q}$ becomes a fraction of elements of that local ring. It feeds the statement [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.forall_exists_isDiscreteValuationRing_specializes_and_mul_stalkRead_eq_stalkRead`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.forall_exists_isDiscreteValuationRing_specializes_and_mul_stalkRead_eq_stalkRead), where the coefficient ring $O'$ and the specialisation are produced rather than assumed.
